          %h2#References References
          %p The assertion by Bohr that all experiments in quantum mechanics must be possible to describe in “classical terms” is in
          %ul
            %li#Bohr49
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Bohr"}> Niels Bohr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Discussion with Einstein on Epistemological Problems in Atomic Physics
                %em Albert Einstein, Philosopher-Scientist
                (Evanston: Library of Living Philosophers) (1949) 201-241 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S1876-0503(08)70379-7"}> doi:10.1016/S1876-0503(08)70379-7
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p “however far the phenomena transcend the scope of classical physical explanation, the account of all evidence must be expressed in classical terms.”
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Bohr"}> Niels Bohr
            ‘s views on quantum mechanics that give the construction of
            %em Bohrification
            its name are reviewed further in
          %ul
            %li#Scheibe73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erhard+Scheibe"}> Erhard Scheibe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bohr’s interpretation of quantum mechanics
              = succeed "," do
                %em The logical analysis of quantum mechanics
          %p
            For more see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics"} interpretation of quantum mechanics
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics#BohrStandpoint"} Bohr’s standpoint
          %p
            Maybe the first article to propose to use
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            for the description of quantum physics is
          %ul
            %li
              Murray Adelman, John Corbett,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Sheaf Model for Intuitionistic Quantum Mechanics
              %strong 3
              (1995) 79-104 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00872949"}> doi:10.1007/BF00872949
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The term
            %em Bohrification
            and the investigations associated with it were initiated in
          %ul
            %li#HeunenLandsmanSpitters09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bohrification of operator algebras and quantum logic
              %strong 186
              3 (2012) 719-752 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2275"}> arXiv:0905.2275
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11229-011-9918-4"} doi;10.1007/s11229-011-9918-4
          %p
            see also related comments in disucssion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Born+rule"} Born rule
            here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Born rule and its interpretation
              = succeed "," do
                %em Compendium of Quantum Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-70626-7_20"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-70626-7_20
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ru.nl/~landsman/Born.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Landsman-BornRule.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#HLSDeep
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bohrification
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deep Beauty – Understanding the Quantum World through Mathematical Innovation
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.3468"} arXiv:0909.3468
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511976971.008"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511976971.008
          %p
            The computation of the internal Gelfand spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ̲
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\Sigma}
            was initiated in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              = succeed "," do
                %em A topos for algebraic quantum theory
              %strong 291
              (2009) 63-110 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.4364"}> arXiv:0709.4364
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s00220-009-0865-6"} doi:10.1007/s00220-009-0865-6
          %p with some results in section 5 and 6 of
          %ul
            %li
              Martijn Caspers,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Gelfand spectra of
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ru.nl/~landsman/scriptieMartijn.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Caspers-GelfandSpectra.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p and completed in
          %ul
            %li
              Sander Wolters,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Contravariant vs covariant quantum logic: A comparison of two topos-theoretic approaches to quantum theory
              %strong 317
              (2013) 3–53 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.2031"}> arXiv:1010.2031
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-012-1652-3"} doi:10.1007/s00220-012-1652-3
          %p An outline of the full proof is given in
          %ul
            %li#HLSW
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The Gelfand spectrum of a noncommutative
                  = succeed "-algebra:" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %strong 90
              (2011) 39-52 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.2050"}> arxiv:1010.2050
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S1446788711001157"} doi:10.1017/S1446788711001157
          %p
            Applications and examples for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            algebra are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Martijn Caspers,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"} Chris Heunen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Intuitionistic Quantum Logic of an
                  = succeed "-level" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %strong 39
              7 (2009) 731-759 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.3201"}> arXiv:0902.3201
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10701-009-9308-7"} doi:10.1007/s10701-009-9308-7
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functoriality
            of Bohrification is observed in
          %ul
            %li#vdBergHeunen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"} Chris Heunen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutativity as a colimit
              %strong 20
              4 (2012) 393-414 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3618"}> arXiv:1003.3618
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-011-9246-3"} doi:10.1007/s10485-011-9246-3
          %p
            The application of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+topology"} double negation topology
            to make Bohrification coincide with ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            on commutative
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
          %ul
            %li#Spitters06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"}> Bas Spitters
